inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Or point the extension’s Info.plist "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSExtensionPrincipalClass"},{"text":" at","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PushwooshNotificationServiceExtension"},{"text":" directly and write no Swift\/Obj-C at all.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Requirements:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Pushwoosh_APPID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in the main app Info.plist. You do not need to duplicate it in the extension","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Info.plist — when missing there, Pushwoosh inherits it (and other ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pushwoosh_*"},{"type":"text","text":" keys) from the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"host app. Set it explicitly in the extension Info.plist only to override the host."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mutable-content: 1"},{"type":"text","text":" in the push payload (so the extension is invoked)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"App Group shared between the app and the extension for badge \/ reverse-proxy sync"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"(set ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PW_APP_GROUPS_NAME"},{"text":" in Info.plist or override ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pushwooshAppGroupsName"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Note: if the host app uses a reverse proxy (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Pushwoosh_ALLOW_REVERSE_PROXY"},{"type":"text","text":"), the extension"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"needs this App Group to read the proxy URL the app stored there — otherwise the delivery event"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is held back (it will not bypass the proxy). Add the App Group capabili